abstract: >-
  This repository contains the computational research infrastructure for a
  comparative in-silico investigation of TP53 mutation-associated hotspots
  across humans and elephants. The project integrates publicly available
  sequence resources, sequence preprocessing, similarity-based sequence
  identification, multiple sequence alignment, mutation-associated residue
  mapping, evolutionary analysis, feature extraction, exploratory
  machine-learning analysis, scientific visualization, and the EleProtect
  interactive research application. The repository is structured to support
  transparent provenance, reproducibility, computational auditability, and
  responsible interpretation of comparative genomics results.

